162
00:56:36,925 --> 00:56:42,921
A sailor 's fallen ill below deck . He 's delirious .

163
00:58:07,405 --> 00:58:10,920
It spread through the ship like an epidemic .

164
00:58:11,045 --> 00:58:14,560
The first stricken sailor pulled the entire crew

165
00:58:14,685 --> 00:58:17,961
after him into the dark grave of the waves .

166
00:58:18,085 --> 00:58:21,521
In the light of the sinking sun ,

167
00:58:21,645 --> 00:58:25,035
the captain and ship ' s mate

168
00:58:25,165 --> 00:58:28,157
bid farewell to the last of their comrades .

169
00:58:56,965 --> 00:59:05,441
I 'm going below ! If I 'm not back up in ten minutes ...

170
01:01:14,845 --> 01:01:20,397
The ship of death had acquired its new captain .

171
01:01:26,765 --> 01:01:28,437
End of the 3rd Act .

172
01:01:29,085 --> 01:01:30,757
Nosferatu 4th Act .

173
01:01:30,885 --> 01:01:34,082
It 's quite difficult to say how , despite his depleted strength ,

174
01:01:34,205 --> 01:01:36,844
young Hutter succeeded in surmounting the obstacles

175
01:01:36,965 --> 01:01:39,195
on his voyage home - - meanwhlle , Nosferatu 's

176
01:01:39,325 --> 01:01:41,520
deadly breath swelled the sails of the ship ,

177
01:01:41,645 --> 01:01:44,557
which flew on toward it 's destination with ghostly haste .

178
01:03:13,205 --> 01:03:16,436
I must go to him . He 's coming !

179
01:05:11,045 --> 01:05:16,244
The master is near ... The master is near !

180
01:06:24,525 --> 01:06:29,235
Long have I pondered why Nosferatu was said

181
01:06:29,365 --> 01:06:34,758
to have travelled with earth-filled coffins .

182
01:06:34,885 --> 01:06:40,482
I found it recorded that vampyres

183
01:06:40,605 --> 01:06:46,043
can only draw their shadowy strength

184
01:06:46,165 --> 01:06:51,637
